It's been almost 12 months since Apple launched the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a>, and because <em>MacRumors</em> videographer Dan Barbera has been using it daily since launch, he decided to do a one-year review covering what it's like using Apple's super-thin iPhone on a long-term basis.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="I Used the iPhone Air for One Year...Here's What I Think" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/YEmYTcakGyA" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; is the thinnest iPhone Apple has released to date, and the form factor doesn't get old. It's pocketable, can be used with one hand, and it's much lighter than the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a> and Pro Max. There's not much compromise on screen size since it has a 6.5-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> display.<br/>
<br/>
Apple used a smaller battery in the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj;, and it doesn't last as long as the &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj; models. Some people might be able to get through the day on a single charge, but others will need an external battery pack like the one Apple built for the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
There's a single camera, which is one of the compromises with Apple's super-thin iPhone. You only get the Wide lens, with no option for the Ultra Wide or Telephoto lenses that come with the other <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a> models. No Ultra Wide also means no macro images.<br/>
<br/>
Price was and continues to be the biggest &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; issue. At &#36;999, it's more expensive than the &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj;, which has two cameras and nearly the same processor, and only &#36;100 less than the three-camera &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj;. The &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj;'s price wasn't worth it to a lot of people, and rumors suggest that it <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/22/iphone-air-supply-chain-cuts/">didn't sell well</a>.<br/>
